# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore (repository root)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker build-context exclusions for every image whose build context is the
# repository ROOT. Today that is exactly one: reporting-service, whose Dockerfile
# compiles the Maven reactor in-container and therefore needs the aggregator
# pom.xml, every module pom.xml, carddemo-common/ and reporting-service/
# (docker-compose.yml: `context: .` + `dockerfile: reporting-service/Dockerfile`).
#
# Docker resolves .dockerignore relative to the CONTEXT root, not the repository
# root, so this file governs root-context builds only. The nine module-context
# builds carry their own <module>/.dockerignore, and the frontend carries
# frontend/.dockerignore.
#
# Why this matters: without any ignore file the root context measured about
# 1.8 GB (host target/ output across ten modules, frontend/node_modules, the
# .git history and a local Maven repository), and every backend build logged
# "load .dockerignore … 2B" with 70-75 MB transferred (QA Issue 20). The image
# CONTENTS were already correct - this is build time, cache hygiene and secret
# hygiene, not a packaging defect.
#
# Kept consistent with the repository-root .gitignore (Respecting .gitignore
# rule, AAP 0.7.2). This file complements .gitignore; it does not replace it,
# because the two answer different questions ("may it be committed?" versus "must
# it be uploaded to the build daemon?").
#
# The following build inputs are intentionally NOT ignored and REMAIN copyable:
#   pom.xml, */pom.xml, carddemo-common/src/, reporting-service/src/
# =============================================================================

# --- Host build output (the reactor is rebuilt inside the image) -------------
# reporting-service/Dockerfile runs `mvn -pl reporting-service -am clean package`
# in its build stage, so no host-produced jar or class file is ever needed.
**/target

# --- Node dependencies and build output (frontend has its own context) -------
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/build
frontend/coverage
frontend/.vite

# --- Version control and CI metadata ----------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Secrets: never upload local environment files to the build daemon ------
# Compose injects every credential as an environment variable at RUN time; no
# secret is ever baked into an image layer.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks

# --- Docker and Kubernetes descriptors (not build inputs) -------------------
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
**/.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
k8s

# --- Local Maven repository, if one was materialized inside the checkout -----
.m2

# --- Retained legacy mainframe sources and reference assets ------------------
# The COBOL/JCL/BMS originals are the transformation reference (AAP 0.2.1) and
# the diagram/sample assets are reference-only (AAP 0.2.2); none is compiled
# into, or copied into, any container image.
app
diagrams
samples

# --- Documentation and observability templates -------------------------------
# Mounted at run time by docker-compose / Kubernetes, never copied into an image.
docs
observability
*.md

# --- Logs, caches and OS/editor cruft ---------------------------------------
*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
*.iml

# --- Transient QA and validation scratch ------------------------------------
# Ad-hoc validation artifacts are prefixed blitzy_adhoc_test_ and are never
# committed; excluding them keeps a working checkout from bloating the context.
blitzy
blitzy_adhoc_test_*
